{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The claim asserts the 2-sigma fairness criterion is violated at n=10000, but the mechanism concedes bias 'could' push faces 1/2 above the bound without establishing that it does. Quantitatively, the per-draw bias is ~1.4e-8 (one surplus pre-image per 2^31 states), so over 10000 draws the expected excess for faces 1 or 2 is ~1.4e-4 counts—negligible versus the ~74-count 2-sigma band. The claim is unsupported: it asserts violation while its own mechanism cannot rule out the third countercondition (bias too small at n=10000), which it lists as observation-pending.","target":"b58f3dfd0053d82c2ed0f29e34b4db49f1f5b6775080b315061fe95aa01c7726"}]}